                <pb facs="0329" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.248/102: Telegram.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-24T11:00:00-04:00">May 24, 1938—11 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>72. Your 124, May 23, 2 p.m. I concur in your opinion. I have discussed the
                    matter very fully with the Brazilian Ambassador here, and he assures me that he
                    is absolutely in accord with our own point of view and has so informed his
                    Government. The point he stresses is that it is far more to the interest of
                    Brazil to have American technical experts in the Argentine army than Germans or
                    Italians.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
